# URL of the statcmd Cloudflare Worker's render route (worker/statcmd.js, the
# `/v3` endpoint). This is the base the customizer puts into every generated
# `$(urlfetch …)` command AND the URL the live chat preview fetches to render.
# It's a public URL, not a secret. For the deployed site set a GitHub Actions
# repository variable named VITE_STATCMD_URL; copy this file to `.env.local` for
# local dev (e.g. point it at `http://localhost:8787/v3` while running
# `wrangler dev`). When left blank the customizer falls back to
# https://statcmd.kapkit.ca/v3 for the command string and shows a sample line in
# the preview instead of calling a Worker.
VITE_STATCMD_URL=

# Optional: PostHog analytics (see src/shared/analytics.ts). Create a free
# project at https://posthog.com, then paste its "Project API Key" (Settings →
# Project → General, starts with `phc_`) here. When set, the customizer loads
# PostHog (cookie-based, gated behind the consent banner) with autocapture,
# pageviews, and named events; leave blank to disable analytics entirely (the app
# works fine without it). The Project API Key is a public, write-only identifier,
# not a secret. For the deployed site set a GitHub Actions repository variable
# named VITE_POSTHOG_KEY.
#
# NOTE: only the *Project API Key* (`phc_…`) goes here. Never put your PostHog
# *Personal API key* in this file or the bundle — it is a server-side credential
# and this app ships to the browser.
VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=
# PostHog API host — match your project's data-residency region:
# https://us.i.posthog.com (US, the default) or https://eu.i.posthog.com (EU).
# Set as a repository variable named VITE_POSTHOG_HOST for the deployed site.
# Optionally point it at a reverse-proxy subdomain of your own domain to dodge
# ad blockers.
VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=
# Optional event-name prefix, applied to every custom event (e.g.
# `statcmd_command_copied`) and also registered as a `site` super property on
# every event — including PostHog's autocaptured ones — so several sites can
# SHARE ONE PostHog project and still be told apart. Defaults to "statcmd".
# Set as a repository variable named VITE_POSTHOG_EVENT_PREFIX to override.
VITE_POSTHOG_EVENT_PREFIX=
